gomodel:6a4c244800005011
        a                 owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment      "Claude: Curation notes / caveats\n- **BRCA1 MF is a judgment call.** Curator chose ubiquitin protein ligase\n  activity (GO:0061630, its EXP-supported MF). The four checkpoint papers read\n  (Yarden 2002; RAP80/Abraxas/MERIT40: PMID:17525340, 17643121, 19261748) do\n  NOT attribute G2/M arrest specifically to BRCA1 catalysis — BRCA1 acts largely\n  as a mediator/scaffold. If challenged, molecular adaptor activity (GO:0060090)\n  is the alternative framing. Relevant: BRCA1-C complex (GO:0070533) is\n  described as \"required for DNA damage-induced Chk1 phosphorylation and the\n  G2/M transition checkpoint.\"\n- **Context-edge evidence** (enabled_by / part_of / occurs_in) was populated\n  with each protein's primary reference for completeness; refine as needed.\n- BRCA1 → CHK1 modeled as *indirect* (i+) — BRCA1 is required for CHK1\n  activation but does not phosphorylate CHK1 directly." ;
        lego:modelstate   "delete" ;
        dc:contributor    "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1813-6857" ;
        dc:date           "2026-07-22" ;
        dc:title          "Example #2 for MF guidelines: sequestering activity" ;
        pav:providedBy    "http://geneontology.org" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom>
                gomodel:63f809ec00000027 ;
        biolink:in_taxon  obo:NCBITaxon_9606 , obo:NCBITaxon_2697049 .

